/*!
    \page qtuniversalinput-index.html
    \title Qt Universal Input
    \brief Provides C++ and QML APIs for reading game controllers, joysticks
    and other input devices.

    Qt Universal Input is an experimental module that provides a cross-platform
    way of reading input from game controllers, joysticks and similar devices.
    Its input layer is derived from the input handling of the Godot engine and
    uses the community \l{https://github.com/mdqinc/SDL_GameControllerDB}
    {SDL game controller database} to map physical devices onto a common gamepad
    layout.

    The repository provides three closely related areas of functionality:

    \list
        \li The \l{Qt Universal Input C++ Classes}{QtUniversalInput} module with
            the low level QUniversalInput singleton and the higher level
            QActionStore for mapping raw input onto named actions.
        \li The \l{Qt Gamepad C++ Classes}{QtGamepad} compatibility module with
            the QGamepad convenience class.
        \li QML modules that expose the same functionality to Qt Quick.
    \endlist

    \section1 Using the Module

    \section2 Using the C++ API

    \include {module-use.qdocinc} {using the c++ api}

    \section2 Using the QML API

    \include {module-use.qdocinc} {using the qml api} {QtUniversalInput}

    \section1 Reference

    \list
        \li \l{Qt Universal Input C++ Classes}
        \li \l{Qt Gamepad C++ Classes}
        \li \l{Qt Universal Input QML Types}
    \endlist

    \section1 Licenses and Attributions

    Qt Universal Input is available under commercial licenses from
